{
  "_readme": [
    "Declarative model state for cloud workers (Colab). One HF repo mirrors",
    "the studio's models/ tree; groups select which subsets a worker pulls.",
    "",
    "PC side: tool/scripts/publish_models_hf.py walks 'source' paths, fills",
    "bytes + sha256, and uploads to hf_repo (private dataset repo).",
    "Worker side: colab/fetch_models.py (bootstrap) or the Worker PCs page",
    "group-install pulls the union of the selected groups into models_dir",
    "with the SAME relative layout, so model filenames in workflows resolve",
    "byte-identically. Files already present with a matching size are",
    "skipped, so re-running after a Colab session death only fetches deltas.",
    "",
    "bytes/sha256 are filled in by the publisher; 0/empty means 'compute at",
    "publish time'. Path is the worker-relative layout (models_dir/<path>).",
    "Disk budget: h3_shared + one h3 DiT ~ 20GB; every extra DiT",
    "group adds ~12GB, ltx_core ~27GB, stills groups 8-15GB."
  ],
